title The lap recovered from the dead-letter box
prompt Autonomous lap, diffuser seat, with the round-open naming six parked paths on no ref.
rota lap 5004, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in; take the concrete fact at the door before any argument about it. The concrete fact was the round-open's own printout: five built files and a log standing in stash@{0} and nowhere else. It outranked every idea I might have opened instead.
think fleet_round_open.sh named the parked paths and stash_record_scan.sh list classified them orphan:work and unlanded -- a whole lap staged and cut at its send twenty minutes earlier.
think The stash base 701f3768f is an ancestor of HEAD, and every file sat in stash@{0}^2 (the index) rather than ^3, so the six added files restore with git checkout stash@{0}^2 -- and the five modified files were re-applied hunk by hunk instead, since HEAD had moved under them.
think Re-ran tools/w/workload_trial_witness.rish on metal before staging: GREEN, 57 legs, control_failed=0.
think The eighth timing reading came back at spread_pct=54.8 against the paper's published 16.7 to 38.0 across seven, so the paper's own closing prediction -- expect a wider one still -- was confirmed by the first reading after it published.
think reranks_recommended read 6 before the erratum landed and 7 after, which is the paper's table figure arriving only once the page it describes carries the row.
obs A cut send leaves no record of itself except the stash. The log claims status GREEN and a completed hot pass; the work never reached a ref. status written before the send is what let this lap tell a finished lap from a killed one at a glance.
obs Landed the parked log at its own stamp rather than folding its words into mine -- it is testimony of the lap that did the work, and this one only carried it across.
obs Swept the stale range across five surfaces rather than one: the paper, the erratum line, the roster comment, the witness header, the witness say line, and the card. A figure declared FREE still has to be the freshest reading a lap actually took.
obs A parked lap re-enters a tree whose ceilings have moved. The control's six sed -i calls were lawful when written and are a red now -- gated_sed_i_ceiling reads 0, walled by a peer while the work sat in the box. Repaired by sourcing tools/fixtures/s/shell_portable.sh and calling sed_inplace; 57 legs still stand.
obs The rebase turned the rung RED for a reason the recovery caused: bearing_quorum_scan.sh moved from the m letter room to the b its own basename computes while this work sat in the stash, so row 8's erratum named an absent instrument. The erratum is testimony and keeps its path, so the scan resolves a stale tools path by recomputing the letter room from the basename -- two-letter room tried second, as tool_path_resolve.rish does. Five new pen legs, both sides planted; 57 to 62.
obs Four reds of the hot pass were mine and all four came from the gap rather than from the work: two dialect walls, and two roster counts where 20260914 read 110 against a shelf holding 114. The other thirteen name no path of mine.
